# to run quicknode_mempool_monitor:
- ensure the following dependencies are installed
	- websocketpp
	- boost
	- openssl@3
	- jsoncpp
	
- then to compile use either of the following two options 
	- use the make file
	> make
	
	- or run "g++ -std=c++17 -I/opt/homebrew/opt/websocketpp/include \
           -I/opt/homebrew/opt/boost/include -I/opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/include \
		   -I/opt/homebrew/opt/jsoncpp/include -L/opt/homebrew/opt/boost/lib -L/opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/lib -L/opt/homebrew/opt/jsoncpp/lib \
          -lboost_system -lssl -lcrypto -ljsoncpp -lcurl -o quicknode_mempool_monitor quicknode_mempool_monitor.cpp"
	
	- run ./quicknode_mempool_monitor <quicknode endpoint HTTPS provider> <count> <p/s>
	
	- EXAMPLES:
		> ./quicknode_mempool_monitor https://mystic-rolling-forest.quiknode.pro/abc123xyz456def789ghi0123 10 p
		- This runs (multithreaded) until 10 transactions to uniswap mempool router are detected then returns time taken.
		
		> ./quicknode_mempool_monitor https://mystic-rolling-forest.quiknode.pro/abc123xyz456def789ghi0123 20 s
		- This runs (serially) until 20 transactions to uniswap mempool router are detected then returns time taken.
	
	This will print out <count> Ethereum transaction hashes going to uniswap mempool and will return time taken to complete.
